1
00:02:03,865 --> 00:02:08,905
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:09,461 --> 00:02:11,031
We are going to İnegöl.

3
00:02:11,066 --> 00:02:12,926
It's about time, Osman Bey.

4
00:02:15,978 --> 00:02:17,458
My bey!

5
00:02:19,805 --> 00:02:21,495
My bey, someone is coming!

6
00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:29,950
Alps, wait!

7
00:02:39,011 --> 00:02:40,911
We saved you from the vizier...

8
00:02:42,722 --> 00:02:44,882
thanks to Kosses.

9
00:03:01,215 --> 00:03:03,395
Welcome, Michael Kosses.

10
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:06,324
Thank you, Osman Bey.

11
00:03:40,743 --> 00:03:42,183
Allah damn it!

12
00:03:42,389 --> 00:03:44,039
What happened here?

13
00:03:44,733 --> 00:03:46,103
Osman.

14
00:03:46,918 --> 00:03:48,788
They ran away.

15
00:03:50,129 --> 00:03:52,652
What is this, Konur Alp?

16
00:03:52,652 --> 00:03:55,082
Couldn't you stop a few men?

17
00:03:55,389 --> 00:03:57,279
They played us.

18
00:03:58,300 --> 00:03:59,906
We tried to stop them but---

19
00:03:59,906 --> 00:04:03,776
But you couldn't stop them even
though you sensed it.

20
00:04:06,074 --> 00:04:09,834
Maybe I overvalue you.

21
00:04:13,131 --> 00:04:16,011
One of the dervishes gave
sherbet to the guards.

22
00:04:18,876 --> 00:04:22,666
When they fell a sleep,
they entered.

23
00:04:22,976 --> 00:04:27,016
But this won't happen again,
my vizier.

24
00:04:27,550 --> 00:04:29,560
A dervish?

25
00:04:30,165 --> 00:04:32,525
I was right.

26
00:04:34,627 --> 00:04:36,247
Edebali...

27
00:04:36,345 --> 00:04:38,875
you are helping Osman, huh?

28
00:04:54,290 --> 00:04:56,680
You are here in time, Celali.

29
00:04:58,526 --> 00:05:03,356
He'll understand what happens
when he works with Osman.

30
00:05:04,556 --> 00:05:07,066
He'll pay for it.

31
00:05:07,911 --> 00:05:09,941
As you order, my vizier.

32
00:05:13,455 --> 00:05:15,355
Pull yourself together.

33
00:05:15,452 --> 00:05:17,382
You'll find Osman.

34
00:05:18,501 --> 00:05:21,241
I won't accept any other mistake.

35
00:05:22,758 --> 00:05:24,748
As you order, my vizier.

36
00:05:32,359 --> 00:05:36,809
We swore a sacred oath to
stand together with the lords.

37
00:05:38,035 --> 00:05:41,265
But this betrayal of
dishonorable Nikola...

38
00:05:41,377 --> 00:05:43,527
overrides my oath.

39
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:51,580
The desire for vengeance
made you work with us, Kosses.

40
00:05:54,607 --> 00:05:56,247
It is.

41
00:05:56,599 --> 00:05:57,859
Osman Bey.

42
00:05:59,853 --> 00:06:01,763
But don't forget.

43
00:06:01,882 --> 00:06:04,152
It's only until we deal with Nikola.

44
00:06:08,459 --> 00:06:10,659
If you say so.

45
00:06:11,848 --> 00:06:13,668
Alright.

46
00:06:14,523 --> 00:06:19,043
But don't you work behind
my back...

47
00:06:19,362 --> 00:06:21,732
under the disguise of vengeance.

48
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,590
Don't worry.

49
00:06:31,196 --> 00:06:34,306
I'll only play with those
who hurt me.

50
00:06:34,441 --> 00:06:36,202
Be at ease.

51
00:06:36,202 --> 00:06:38,332
I always am.

52
00:06:40,787 --> 00:06:42,167
Both on games...

53
00:06:43,078 --> 00:06:44,818
and traps.

54
00:06:45,562 --> 00:06:47,422
Don't worry.

55
00:06:48,701 --> 00:06:49,811
But...

56
00:06:50,986 --> 00:06:52,916
I say that...

57
00:06:53,418 --> 00:06:57,768
it's my people's good that will
be on the markets.

58
00:06:58,252 --> 00:07:00,332
And there are your goods.

59
00:07:01,013 --> 00:07:03,153
I don't want them to get
harmed.

60
00:07:04,352 --> 00:07:06,782
This market in İnegöl...

61
00:07:07,204 --> 00:07:11,054
isn't good for you or me.

62
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,040
We'll destroy that market.

63
00:07:15,312 --> 00:07:16,892
I understand.

64
00:07:17,774 --> 00:07:20,584
So, what do you want from me?

65
00:07:20,796 --> 00:07:22,996
Your goods are going there too.

66
00:07:23,414 --> 00:07:25,194
The cart that will take them...

67
00:07:25,661 --> 00:07:29,631
will carry the alps and the
oil that will burn the market down.

68
00:07:30,904 --> 00:07:33,744
We'll burn them down.

69
00:07:36,019 --> 00:07:39,659
A lord incapable of protecting
his own lands...

70
00:07:39,859 --> 00:07:42,889
can't own such a market.

71
00:07:44,859 --> 00:07:46,829
And then?

72
00:07:47,948 --> 00:07:52,208
When the vizier has no choice, he'll
set the market in Harmankaya.

73
00:07:56,175 --> 00:07:57,965
You thought well.

74
00:07:58,376 --> 00:08:04,006
But neither the vizier nor the Nikola
would ever want that.

75
00:08:06,751 --> 00:08:10,171
The market won't be in Harmankaya...

76
00:08:10,391 --> 00:08:12,401
but in a better place,
Bilecik.

77
00:08:12,557 --> 00:08:17,217
And I'll tell them about the benefits
of having the market in Bilecik.

78
00:08:18,242 --> 00:08:22,522
And Rogatus? Will you
be able to control him?

79
00:08:24,713 --> 00:08:27,293
To revenge from Nikola...

80
00:08:27,393 --> 00:08:30,113
I can even convince the devil.

81
00:08:35,321 --> 00:08:36,931
Alright.

82
00:08:37,952 --> 00:08:39,362
Alright.

83
00:08:40,177 --> 00:08:42,377
The market will be in Bilecik.

84
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:44,430
You'll confront the vizier.

85
00:08:45,397 --> 00:08:48,847
And I'll finish off that dishonorable
Nikola...

86
00:08:49,168 --> 00:08:52,528
who tried to kill my Mari.

87
00:08:53,856 --> 00:08:56,686
We all will get what we want.

88
00:09:04,575 --> 00:09:06,505
Mari is with us.

89
00:09:09,876 --> 00:09:11,976
You returned from your mistake.

90
00:09:16,372 --> 00:09:17,882
Mari.

91
00:09:18,791 --> 00:09:21,351
We should get your brother's approval.

92
00:09:28,712 --> 00:09:30,682
With Allah's order...

93
00:09:31,307 --> 00:09:35,137
and our holy prophet's words...

94
00:09:39,434 --> 00:09:41,394
we ask for your
sister Maria...

95
00:09:42,508 --> 00:09:45,258
for my brother Turgut.

96
00:10:00,541 --> 00:10:02,241
With one condition

97
00:10:09,601 --> 00:10:11,701
The wedding will be at Harmankaya.

98
00:10:19,533 --> 00:10:21,493
Alright.

99
00:10:22,049 --> 00:10:24,109
Let it be Harmankaya.

100
00:10:26,355 --> 00:10:29,595
Then, I allow my sister Mari...

101
00:10:29,909 --> 00:10:33,239
to marry Turgut Bey.

102
00:10:40,739 --> 00:10:42,249
Thank you.

103
00:10:45,422 --> 00:10:47,092
Thank you.

104
00:10:54,496 --> 00:10:55,906
Mari.

105
00:10:58,856 --> 00:11:00,446
Brother.

106
00:11:10,048 --> 00:11:11,898
My dear.

107
00:11:13,112 --> 00:11:15,722
I always wanted the best for you.

108
00:11:21,199 --> 00:11:23,629
After the market burns...

109
00:11:23,806 --> 00:11:27,936
you can't stay here. All eyes
will be on you.

110
00:11:28,027 --> 00:11:31,057
So, I'll host you at Harmankaya.

111
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:35,810
Let's take care of this İnegöl
issue first.

112
00:11:50,243 --> 00:11:52,323
My friend Zehra.

113
00:11:52,448 --> 00:11:54,598
One of the tribeswomen.

114
00:12:00,186 --> 00:12:01,966
Sheik Edebalı!

115
00:12:08,036 --> 00:12:09,766
While we were here...

116
00:12:09,981 --> 00:12:14,761
Osman avoided my soldiers, took his alps
and left.

117
00:12:17,477 --> 00:12:20,317
Are you aware of that?

118
00:12:25,268 --> 00:12:29,608
My soldiers passed out because
of a sherbet...

119
00:12:29,644 --> 00:12:31,784
given by ahis.

120
00:12:33,615 --> 00:12:36,525
You did an unjust thing.

121
00:12:37,488 --> 00:12:39,568
Without a proof...

122
00:12:40,090 --> 00:12:43,590
you threw the alps
to the dungeon.

123
00:12:44,647 --> 00:12:46,557
Osman Bey...

124
00:12:46,969 --> 00:12:49,279
was assuring justice...

125
00:12:49,739 --> 00:12:51,859
and I stood by him.

126
00:12:52,037 --> 00:12:53,917
And I always will.

127
00:12:54,352 --> 00:12:56,892
You will regret that, Edebalı.

128
00:12:57,162 --> 00:12:59,852
You will pay dearly for it.

129
00:13:00,574 --> 00:13:02,424
If the price is...

130
00:13:02,951 --> 00:13:06,961
our lives leaving our bodies...

131
00:13:07,404 --> 00:13:09,534
don't hold back.

132
00:13:10,103 --> 00:13:14,303
What you see as a punishment
is an award for us.

133
00:13:15,427 --> 00:13:20,017
What you see as an award
is a punishment for us.

134
00:13:21,036 --> 00:13:25,076
Arrest the rebellious sheik!

135
00:13:25,235 --> 00:13:28,345
-Leave the sheik!
-Leave him! My Sheik!

136
00:13:28,789 --> 00:13:32,029
Let our sheik go!

137
00:13:32,166 --> 00:13:34,216
Bala Hatun!

138
00:13:35,679 --> 00:13:38,448
-Bala!
-Why are you taking my father?

139
00:13:38,448 --> 00:13:40,164
What will you do to him?

140
00:13:40,164 --> 00:13:41,734
Don't worry.

141
00:13:42,193 --> 00:13:46,273
I'll leave your father
to a professional.

142
00:13:57,077 --> 00:13:58,587
-Let him go!
-My sweetheart.

143
00:13:59,473 --> 00:14:02,003
My sweetheart, stop.

144
00:14:04,116 --> 00:14:06,646
Whatever comes from our Allah...

145
00:14:06,831 --> 00:14:08,931
is a gift.

146
00:14:11,730 --> 00:14:13,480
Wait.

147
00:14:14,069 --> 00:14:16,359
Be patient.

148
00:14:17,882 --> 00:14:19,622
Take him!

149
00:14:19,782 --> 00:14:23,392
No! No, father!
Let my father go!

150
00:14:23,558 --> 00:14:26,408
Father! Let him go!

151
00:14:26,437 --> 00:14:27,997
My sheik!

152
00:14:32,619 --> 00:14:34,219
Father...

153
00:14:35,302 --> 00:14:36,922
Father...

154
00:14:38,290 --> 00:14:40,900
Oh, my lion son.

155
00:14:46,638 --> 00:14:48,598
All the troubles we have...

156
00:14:51,531 --> 00:14:54,361
is endured because I have
you in my heart.

157
00:14:58,036 --> 00:15:00,686
Your shining eyes...

158
00:15:04,060 --> 00:15:07,630
I live to let them see further
from these lands.

159
00:15:11,050 --> 00:15:12,900
My Orhan.

160
00:15:19,314 --> 00:15:21,144
Mashallah.

161
00:15:21,284 --> 00:15:24,074
He'll be as valiant as
his father, inshallah.

162
00:15:24,286 --> 00:15:27,146
He will.
He will, Malhun.

163
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:37,760
You look kindly at Orhan.

164
00:15:37,882 --> 00:15:40,322
Look how they love him.

165
00:15:40,612 --> 00:15:42,822
Both their eyes are shining.

166
00:15:45,933 --> 00:15:47,703
Orhan is very lucky.

167
00:15:49,105 --> 00:15:51,445
So will be our child.

168
00:15:52,861 --> 00:15:55,011
After I have a child...

169
00:15:55,555 --> 00:15:58,975
I'll look at my child in a way
that my eyes will shine like stars.

170
00:16:01,155 --> 00:16:03,705
Just as it shines when
I look at you.

171
00:16:04,159 --> 00:16:05,939
I hope so, Turgut.

172
00:16:08,422 --> 00:16:09,772
My bey.

173
00:16:10,523 --> 00:16:13,133
Take him.

174
00:16:17,089 --> 00:16:18,949
Baysungur.

175
00:16:19,147 --> 00:16:21,917
My bey, Vizier Alemşah!

176
00:16:23,125 --> 00:16:25,605
He arrested Sheik Edebalı...

177
00:16:25,944 --> 00:16:27,664
and threw him to the dungeon.

178
00:16:37,948 --> 00:16:40,298
They are attacking...

179
00:16:40,605 --> 00:16:42,565
and now the dungeon!

180
00:16:44,572 --> 00:16:46,552
My sheik!

181
00:16:52,046 --> 00:16:55,586
My bey, allow me to go and
accompany my sheik.

182
00:16:56,108 --> 00:16:58,758
-Allow me, my bey.
-Kumral Abdal!

183
00:16:59,015 --> 00:17:00,495
Wait.

184
00:17:01,307 --> 00:17:06,307
My bey, allow me to cut their throats!

185
00:17:06,690 --> 00:17:09,230
Cerkutay, wait.

186
00:17:09,323 --> 00:17:12,673
My bey, allow me to
take his head!

187
00:17:12,789 --> 00:17:14,769
Allow me, my bey!

188
00:17:14,769 --> 00:17:17,609
Alps! Wait!

189
00:17:18,707 --> 00:17:20,517
Wait!

190
00:17:23,056 --> 00:17:25,036
The one who does that
to ulema...

191
00:17:26,927 --> 00:17:29,347
is the greatest traitor.

192
00:17:33,409 --> 00:17:35,939
The vizier wants us to do that.

193
00:17:37,727 --> 00:17:41,997
He wants us to enter the
dungeon and take our sheik.

194
00:17:46,264 --> 00:17:48,144
But...

195
00:17:54,234 --> 00:17:56,364
we won't do that.

196
00:17:57,197 --> 00:17:59,757
we'll lead the folk to a revolt.

197
00:18:02,626 --> 00:18:04,136
Turgut Bey.

198
00:18:04,305 --> 00:18:06,085
Go to Söğüt.

199
00:18:06,758 --> 00:18:09,058
All the people are loyal to my sheik.

200
00:18:09,149 --> 00:18:13,439
Tell them that they shouldn't stop
until the tyrant's cruelty ends.

201
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,810
It's your duty.

202
00:18:16,847 --> 00:18:18,497
Alright, Osman Bey.

203
00:18:21,306 --> 00:18:23,036
-Malhun.
-My bey.

204
00:18:24,604 --> 00:18:26,184
Go to the tribe.

205
00:18:26,359 --> 00:18:28,502
Keep your eyes on my brother.

206
00:18:28,502 --> 00:18:30,152
As you order, my bey.

207
00:18:33,288 --> 00:18:35,058
Alps!

208
00:18:37,609 --> 00:18:41,579
It's time to cut down the
tyrant!

209
00:18:42,266 --> 00:18:44,046
We are going to İnegöl.

210
00:18:44,186 --> 00:18:46,686
As you order, my bey.

211
00:19:05,633 --> 00:19:08,823
No... No! No!
Not this.

212
00:19:08,833 --> 00:19:11,973
Take this off. I want to take
the best to the market.

213
00:19:15,354 --> 00:19:18,614
Oh, my dear friend Kosses!
Welcome!

214
00:19:23,846 --> 00:19:26,886
Julia, allow us.

215
00:19:27,528 --> 00:19:29,788
As you want, Lord Rogatus.

216
00:19:30,061 --> 00:19:31,301
You too.

217
00:19:39,795 --> 00:19:41,475
We have a problem.

218
00:19:42,328 --> 00:19:43,868
What is it?

219
00:19:44,483 --> 00:19:46,793
Nikola and the vizier.

220
00:19:47,013 --> 00:19:49,073
They have secret agreements.

221
00:19:50,507 --> 00:19:55,357
Why didn't I think this before?
They are old friends.

222
00:19:55,667 --> 00:19:57,117
That's why.

223
00:19:57,814 --> 00:19:59,674
What's why?

224
00:19:59,903 --> 00:20:04,388
That's why Nikola wants to be with
the vizier and take us out.

225
00:20:06,628 --> 00:20:08,708
Understand it, Rogatus.

226
00:20:09,033 --> 00:20:12,153
Even his share is twice of ours.

227
00:20:13,890 --> 00:20:16,140
And tell me.

228
00:20:16,174 --> 00:20:18,624
Why is the market in İnegöl?

229
00:20:20,771 --> 00:20:25,761
Remember how he talked when we
objected to Nikola.

230
00:20:28,870 --> 00:20:32,620
They are using us, Rogatus.

231
00:20:32,745 --> 00:20:36,635
He'll strengthen Nikola economically
by using us.

232
00:20:37,229 --> 00:20:41,749
Then, the stronger Nikola will unite with
the Vizier and destroy us.

233
00:20:41,989 --> 00:20:43,319
Look at this.

234
00:20:43,750 --> 00:20:45,040
I understand.

235
00:20:46,254 --> 00:20:49,744
By taking twice the share,
they'll remove us from the market.

236
00:20:51,789 --> 00:20:53,789
I talked to a merchant.

237
00:20:54,058 --> 00:20:55,458
Rogatus.

238
00:20:55,666 --> 00:20:59,976
Nikola ordered a great amount
of swords and shields.

239
00:21:01,383 --> 00:21:04,005
And he is recruiting soldiers
from the villages.

240
00:21:04,015 --> 00:21:05,355
Think about it.

241
00:21:05,572 --> 00:21:09,942
He already ordered some before
even getting his share.

242
00:21:11,867 --> 00:21:13,147
And, Rogatus.

243
00:21:13,265 --> 00:21:15,425
Do you think Vizier Alemşah...

244
00:21:15,815 --> 00:21:19,405
would allow Nikola to
attack the Turks?

245
00:21:21,308 --> 00:21:24,428
Speak more clearly, Kosses.
Speak more clearly!!

246
00:21:26,478 --> 00:21:28,458
Let me be clear.

247
00:21:28,687 --> 00:21:30,237
Lord Rogatus.

248
00:21:31,028 --> 00:21:32,668
Those swords...

249
00:21:34,762 --> 00:21:37,192
if they can't spill Turkish blood...

250
00:21:38,024 --> 00:21:40,064
whose blood will they spill?

251
00:21:52,774 --> 00:21:54,774
What do you offer to do?

252
00:21:55,523 --> 00:21:57,043
I don't know.

253
00:21:57,525 --> 00:22:00,265
The balance can change at any moment
in these lands.

254
00:22:01,858 --> 00:22:04,458
But of course, we'll get a chance.

255
00:22:07,970 --> 00:22:09,650
Of course, we will.

256
00:22:18,242 --> 00:22:19,392
Allah.

257
00:22:20,170 --> 00:22:21,560
Allah.

258
00:22:22,881 --> 00:22:26,031
Allah. Allah.

259
00:22:26,302 --> 00:22:27,942
Allah.

260
00:22:31,195 --> 00:22:34,255
I remembered the great imam, Akça.

261
00:22:35,328 --> 00:22:40,548
That holy person suffered so much
for speaking the truth.

262
00:22:43,625 --> 00:22:48,815
Ulema has never bowed
against the tyrants.

263
00:22:50,571 --> 00:22:55,181
And we'll walk on the path
we know to be righteous.

264
00:22:57,247 --> 00:23:00,477
We won't turn our back to
the turth...

265
00:23:00,752 --> 00:23:03,992
because of fearing the
tyrant vizier.

266
00:23:04,226 --> 00:23:06,366
Thank Allah, my sheik.

267
00:23:06,515 --> 00:23:08,725
We can stand against the tyrant.

268
00:24:11,788 --> 00:24:16,088
Now, start speaking, sheik.

269
00:24:16,818 --> 00:24:18,962
Where is Osman?

270
00:24:30,493 --> 00:24:33,450
Don't touch my sheik!
Or you'll have a broken hand!

271
00:24:33,450 --> 00:24:36,350
Hit me! Don't touch my sheik.

272
00:24:44,968 --> 00:24:47,308
Until you tell me where
Osman is...

273
00:24:47,890 --> 00:24:51,810
I'll rip your skin
off your bones.

274
00:25:05,562 --> 00:25:07,542
Go ahead.

275
00:25:07,696 --> 00:25:10,126
Speak to the people.

276
00:25:10,224 --> 00:25:11,824
As you order, my bey.

277
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:13,720
Come on.

278
00:25:24,002 --> 00:25:26,022
Salam Alaikum.

279
00:25:26,089 --> 00:25:28,099
Alaikum Salam.

280
00:25:28,511 --> 00:25:30,251
It's Osman Bey's order.

281
00:25:30,492 --> 00:25:32,792
Tomorrow, no one will open
their shops.

282
00:25:32,885 --> 00:25:35,105
They'll stop the production.

283
00:25:37,115 --> 00:25:39,165
-Alright.
-Alright.

284
00:25:40,861 --> 00:25:43,928
Vizier Alemşah put our
vizier in the dungeon.

285
00:25:43,928 --> 00:25:47,568
We can't leave our sheik
in the dungeon! We must do something.

286
00:25:47,989 --> 00:25:52,029
They put our sheik in the dungeon!
How could they?

287
00:25:53,349 --> 00:25:56,449
How can they do that?

288
00:25:56,638 --> 00:25:59,858
How can they put our sheik
in the dungeon? Traitors!

289
00:26:00,049 --> 00:26:01,699
Is this just?

290
00:26:02,093 --> 00:26:04,433
How can this happen?

291
00:26:04,503 --> 00:26:06,133
Traitors!

292
00:26:07,046 --> 00:26:09,456
This can't happen!

293
00:26:13,136 --> 00:26:15,426
You can't put Sheik Edebali
on the dungeon!

294
00:26:22,463 --> 00:26:24,438
You can't do this!

295
00:26:48,805 --> 00:26:51,915
I think you should speak, sheik.

296
00:26:52,504 --> 00:26:54,294
It's your turn now.

297
00:26:54,841 --> 00:26:57,861
Instead of speaking to a tyrant...

298
00:26:58,716 --> 00:27:01,666
I rather spend all my
life in this dungeon.

299
00:27:01,829 --> 00:27:04,739
We gave you more than enough time,
sheik!

300
00:27:15,015 --> 00:27:16,725
What are you doing?

301
00:27:16,930 --> 00:27:19,240
How can you hit Sheik Edebali?

302
00:27:19,474 --> 00:27:22,894
It's Vizier Alemşah's order.
If he doesn't speak...

303
00:27:23,079 --> 00:27:25,714
I'm allowed to do what's
needed.

304
00:27:25,714 --> 00:27:28,064
Then, you'll wait, Celali!

305
00:27:28,086 --> 00:27:30,836
Sheik Edebali will speak
when he wants to.

306
00:27:30,836 --> 00:27:32,756
And you will wait.

307
00:27:34,311 --> 00:27:36,671
But you won't hit him.

308
00:27:37,128 --> 00:27:39,518
Sheik Edebali is a friend to Allah.

309
00:27:40,587 --> 00:27:44,247
The hand you raise against him can
fall any moment.

310
00:27:49,436 --> 00:27:51,146
Now, leave!

311
00:28:04,913 --> 00:28:07,393
Soldier, give me the keys.

312
00:28:22,093 --> 00:28:24,743
Sheik Edebali, are you alright?

313
00:28:53,193 --> 00:28:55,782
Sheik Edebali, are you alright?

314
00:29:01,208 --> 00:29:03,538
What are you doing...

315
00:29:03,775 --> 00:29:05,675
under Yezid's command, son?

316
00:29:57,940 --> 00:30:01,510
Rogatus is confused enough, Osman Bey.

317
00:30:01,675 --> 00:30:06,125
After we burn their market in İnegöl,
he'll be convinced.

318
00:30:08,839 --> 00:30:13,199
Let's enter İnegöl with
your carts...

319
00:30:13,974 --> 00:30:18,194
and burn the market.
After flames rise...

320
00:30:18,580 --> 00:30:21,380
Rogatus will be convinced.

321
00:30:23,522 --> 00:30:27,242
After burning it, we can fight
our way out, my bey.

322
00:30:28,396 --> 00:30:32,766
Yes. Those who survive do survive.
Those who don't will be martyrs.

323
00:30:33,096 --> 00:30:34,619
Right, brothers?

324
00:30:34,619 --> 00:30:36,781
We missed fighting, my bey.

325
00:30:36,781 --> 00:30:38,308
We are itching, my bey.

326
00:30:38,308 --> 00:30:40,228
May Allah bless our jihad, my bey.

327
00:30:40,292 --> 00:30:41,692
Mashallah.

328
00:30:42,669 --> 00:30:44,679
Mashallah.

329
00:30:45,751 --> 00:30:50,051
If I hadn't seen it with my eyes,
heard it with my ears...

330
00:30:51,167 --> 00:30:53,147
I wouldn't believe it, Osman Bey.

331
00:30:53,965 --> 00:30:56,785
You are lucky to have
such brave soldiers.

332
00:30:57,128 --> 00:31:00,138
This is what you are missing.

333
00:31:00,955 --> 00:31:03,445
They aren't soldiers.

334
00:31:04,250 --> 00:31:06,790
They brothers and comrades
to one other...

335
00:31:07,186 --> 00:31:09,256
their hearts are filled
with faith...

336
00:31:09,543 --> 00:31:13,103
they are Kayı alps!

337
00:31:16,498 --> 00:31:18,468
Alright.

338
00:31:18,599 --> 00:31:22,519
Then, I'll do everything I can to
take this small...

339
00:31:22,568 --> 00:31:27,028
but brave army out of İnegöl alive.

340
00:31:39,341 --> 00:31:41,631
I know the way.

341
00:31:42,993 --> 00:31:45,053
You thought well, Kosses.

342
00:31:46,151 --> 00:31:47,771
You thought well.

343
00:31:56,201 --> 00:31:58,051
Alps.

344
00:32:01,683 --> 00:32:03,943
You'll be cautious.

345
00:32:04,394 --> 00:32:06,744
You'll check everywhere.

346
00:32:06,869 --> 00:32:10,909
But no one will get hurt.

347
00:32:12,787 --> 00:32:18,697
You'll memorize the walls, houses,
towers and even the ground.

348
00:32:20,609 --> 00:32:24,309
They'll help us during our conquest.

349
00:32:25,260 --> 00:32:26,619
As you order, my bey.

350
00:32:26,619 --> 00:32:29,199
-Alright, my bey.
-Alright.

351
00:32:29,843 --> 00:32:33,873
We started the jihad as
soon as we came, Osman Bey.

352
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:36,100
Mashallah to my valiant.

353
00:32:38,955 --> 00:32:40,735
Come on, alps.

354
00:32:54,808 --> 00:32:57,368
İnegöl Castle

355
00:33:05,909 --> 00:33:08,479
These are all examples.

356
00:33:11,048 --> 00:33:14,218
This iron is from Harmankaya.

357
00:33:20,162 --> 00:33:23,412
Our gems are from Bilecik.

358
00:33:27,068 --> 00:33:30,098
And the leathers will be from İnegöl.

359
00:33:34,358 --> 00:33:35,538
And this...

360
00:33:36,110 --> 00:33:38,900
as the symbol of the capable
smiths of the Turks...

361
00:33:39,242 --> 00:33:41,062
from Söğüt.

362
00:33:42,975 --> 00:33:45,065
You thought well, Nikola.

363
00:33:45,389 --> 00:33:49,659
But our smiths don't forge with
anything but our own iron.

364
00:33:50,151 --> 00:33:51,952
Gündüz Bey.

365
00:33:51,952 --> 00:33:55,392
We are in a new order now.

366
00:33:55,558 --> 00:34:00,848
When the capable smiths of the Turks
realize how much they can profit...

367
00:34:01,759 --> 00:34:05,489
they'll change their minds.

368
00:34:14,228 --> 00:34:15,948
Alright.

369
00:34:18,980 --> 00:34:23,330
With these materials,
we'll make the strongest...

370
00:34:23,330 --> 00:34:27,220
sharpest, best swords
of the world!

371
00:34:28,788 --> 00:34:31,588
But is it enough?
It isn't!

372
00:34:31,748 --> 00:34:36,138
At the same time, we'll make the
best sheaths.

373
00:34:38,653 --> 00:34:41,773
It seems like you lived for this moment.

374
00:34:41,898 --> 00:34:44,208
You were so enthusiastic.

375
00:34:44,697 --> 00:34:47,147
Let's not say I lived
for this moment but...

376
00:34:48,422 --> 00:34:50,562
let's say I waited for Vizier Alemşah.

377
00:34:50,905 --> 00:34:53,585
We owe it all to him.

378
00:34:54,035 --> 00:34:55,595
Vizier Alemşah.

379
00:34:55,822 --> 00:35:00,872
I'm grateful that you showed us
how strong we are together.

380
00:35:01,428 --> 00:35:05,287
Once we hold that sheath together,
Nikola...

381
00:35:05,287 --> 00:35:09,227
then, we'll be even stronger.

382
00:35:25,737 --> 00:35:30,207
Osman took his alps from the dungeon.

383
00:35:31,267 --> 00:35:36,385
He took his alps but soon his alps will
be without a bey.

384
00:35:37,004 --> 00:35:41,254
Osman entered a road that he
can't return.

385
00:35:41,625 --> 00:35:44,005
He'll pay dearly.

386
00:35:48,303 --> 00:35:52,683
You know the importance of this market
as much as I do, Nikola.

387
00:35:53,353 --> 00:35:57,853
But I don't want any weakness.

388
00:35:58,796 --> 00:36:01,436
That's on me.

389
00:36:02,032 --> 00:36:05,362
Even a fly can't fly without
getting noticed by me.

390
00:36:06,975 --> 00:36:08,905
But, Vizier Alemşah...

391
00:36:09,269 --> 00:36:11,199
I have a little question.

392
00:36:13,944 --> 00:36:16,374
I wanted to kill Mari.

393
00:36:16,902 --> 00:36:18,332
So...

394
00:36:20,069 --> 00:36:22,879
Turgut took her from me.

395
00:36:24,036 --> 00:36:25,886
Nikola.

396
00:36:26,158 --> 00:36:28,268
Does Kosses know that?

397
00:36:28,578 --> 00:36:30,488
We'll see...

398
00:36:30,751 --> 00:36:34,461
if he loses to his anger when
he comes here...

399
00:36:35,228 --> 00:36:38,488
he might hurt our
mutual interests.

400
00:36:41,052 --> 00:36:45,152
Vizier Alemşah, are you with me?

401
00:36:46,642 --> 00:36:50,312
Take care of the market now.
We'll talk.

402
00:37:09,254 --> 00:37:11,934
Where is my dear friend Kosses?

403
00:37:17,613 --> 00:37:20,703
We did our part.

404
00:37:21,572 --> 00:37:24,512
The rest is on the people
of Söğüt.

405
00:37:25,531 --> 00:37:28,171
Don't worry, Turgut Bey.

406
00:37:28,837 --> 00:37:31,557
The people won't return before
saving our sheik.

407
00:37:31,732 --> 00:37:33,952
-In peace.
-Thank you:

408
00:37:34,068 --> 00:37:35,638
To the forest, alps!

409
00:37:54,397 --> 00:37:56,987
Soldiers! Bring the horses.

410
00:39:14,922 --> 00:39:17,865
I apologize, my friends.
I'm late.

411
00:39:17,865 --> 00:39:20,605
I hope I didn't miss anything important.

412
00:39:21,492 --> 00:39:23,332
Welcome, Kosses.

413
00:39:23,699 --> 00:39:26,004
You didn't miss much.

414
00:39:26,004 --> 00:39:29,974
The Vizier and Nikola took care of all.
They didn't leave anything to us!

415
00:39:30,213 --> 00:39:31,813
-Right, Nikola?
-Yes.

416
00:39:32,180 --> 00:39:35,520
After all, you are my guests.

417
00:39:37,581 --> 00:39:40,411
We are grateful, Nikola.

418
00:39:48,397 --> 00:39:49,977
Come on.

419
00:40:00,950 --> 00:40:02,610
Alps.

420
00:40:31,127 --> 00:40:33,417
So... where is Mari?

421
00:40:35,920 --> 00:40:37,580
Why are you alone?

422
00:40:38,295 --> 00:40:42,471
Mari has gone to make preparations
of our wedding.

423
00:40:42,471 --> 00:40:44,481
She is in Constantinie.

424
00:40:45,248 --> 00:40:49,988
You sent her alone while
our enemies are following us.

425
00:40:54,013 --> 00:40:58,063
I'll break your head if something
happens to her, my friend.

426
00:41:11,440 --> 00:41:13,800
How low you are!

427
00:41:14,024 --> 00:41:15,644
Nicola.

428
00:41:15,920 --> 00:41:19,050
You lie to me in the face!

429
00:41:19,494 --> 00:41:22,204
You have a short time left.

430
00:41:27,076 --> 00:41:29,456
How are you, Gündüz Bey?

431
00:41:30,688 --> 00:41:32,478
Thank you, Lord Kosses.

432
00:41:33,844 --> 00:41:36,394
I heard that Osman got his Alps back.

433
00:41:36,734 --> 00:41:38,734
Does that fear you?

434
00:41:44,111 --> 00:41:46,611
Osman disobeys.

435
00:41:46,979 --> 00:41:49,409
But I am not afraid of my brother.

436
00:41:50,296 --> 00:41:51,886
Of course.

437
00:41:55,834 --> 00:41:57,574
Let's eat!

438
00:41:58,026 --> 00:42:00,005
It's time to eat.

439
00:42:00,005 --> 00:42:01,605
Let's go into the castle.

440
00:44:03,229 --> 00:44:04,709
Soldier!

441
00:44:07,900 --> 00:44:10,230
What is this?
What's happening?

442
00:44:10,347 --> 00:44:13,347
Osman!
This is Osman's job!

443
00:44:38,181 --> 00:44:40,841
Because of you!

444
00:44:41,204 --> 00:44:43,304
You did it!
It's because of you!

445
00:44:45,238 --> 00:44:47,557
You let Osman in!

446
00:44:47,557 --> 00:44:51,237
Watch your mouth, Nikola!
I am here for the wealth of my people!

447
00:44:51,331 --> 00:44:52,953
Why would I harm the market?

448
00:44:52,953 --> 00:44:55,764
Why did I trust a Kayi?

449
00:44:55,764 --> 00:44:58,546
I should have never trusted a Turk!
Never!

450
00:44:58,546 --> 00:45:00,556
Nikola, watch your words!

451
00:45:00,556 --> 00:45:03,746
Don't put the blame on Gündüz Bey
because of your carelessness!

452
00:45:03,746 --> 00:45:05,956
I vouch for his loyalty!

453
00:45:16,558 --> 00:45:19,868
Here is the opportunity.

454
00:45:20,253 --> 00:45:22,803
We need to turn the tables on us.

455
00:45:26,681 --> 00:45:29,341
Tell them to set the market in Bilecik.

456
00:45:30,093 --> 00:45:33,073
We have to break Nikola's power.

457
00:45:36,629 --> 00:45:39,409
Do you see what your brother did,
Gündüz Bey?

458
00:45:39,572 --> 00:45:42,792
It can't be Osman!
I can't believe it!

459
00:45:42,966 --> 00:45:45,093
Why would he want to harm his own people?

460
00:45:45,093 --> 00:45:47,762
Who else could it be other than Osman,
Gündüz Bey?

461
00:45:47,762 --> 00:45:52,242
He wants to ruin the market and
damage our honor.

462
00:45:52,448 --> 00:45:56,728
He doesn't see what's good for his people.

463
00:45:57,087 --> 00:46:01,557
What I want from you to tell your people
about what Osman has done here!

464
00:46:01,688 --> 00:46:05,528
Osman is a rebel who doesn't care
about the wealth of his people!

465
00:47:18,795 --> 00:47:20,570
My Bey, go.
We'll handle.

466
00:47:20,570 --> 00:47:24,410
All for one, one for all, Kutan.

467
00:47:26,099 --> 00:47:27,999
Where are you going, Turgut Bey?

468
00:47:30,302 --> 00:47:32,152
Come on now.

469
00:47:32,181 --> 00:47:34,301
I have been waiting for this moment.

470
00:49:08,835 --> 00:49:10,835
Hay Masha Allah (praise be)

471
00:49:10,875 --> 00:49:12,945
Your breath shall burst, my valiant.

472
00:49:14,515 --> 00:49:16,555
Thank you, Kumral Abdal.

473
00:49:18,002 --> 00:49:19,792
Masha Allah. (praise be!)

474
00:49:20,072 --> 00:49:21,902
Masha Allah. (praise be!)

475
00:49:24,053 --> 00:49:26,383
You have a gifted occupation.

476
00:49:28,429 --> 00:49:31,919
Don't take me wrong, but are you
talking about shepherding?

477
00:49:33,211 --> 00:49:35,121
Yes, Mari Hatun.

478
00:49:35,866 --> 00:49:38,786
Shepherding is sacred.

479
00:49:42,486 --> 00:49:47,236
Our prophet Hadrat Mohammed was a
shepherd too.

480
00:49:50,576 --> 00:49:53,866
Not only our prophet...

481
00:49:55,218 --> 00:49:57,108
Not only him...

482
00:49:59,100 --> 00:50:01,580
But also Abel, son of Hadrat Adam.

483
00:50:01,805 --> 00:50:05,145
Prophet Moses, Prophet David.

484
00:50:05,786 --> 00:50:07,696
They were shepherds too.

485
00:50:08,045 --> 00:50:09,565
Right.

486
00:50:13,457 --> 00:50:16,807
Muhammed, whose name and self is beautiful
said...

487
00:50:17,858 --> 00:50:23,108
...''Allah did not send any prophet who
was not a shepherd.''

488
00:50:24,263 --> 00:50:29,193
The companions asked,
"You too, the Prophet of Allah?"

489
00:50:30,083 --> 00:50:31,363
He said ''Yes...

490
00:50:32,789 --> 00:50:36,919
...once I was a shepherd in Mekka.''

491
00:50:38,478 --> 00:50:40,848
Why is shepherding so important?

492
00:50:44,489 --> 00:50:46,879
Shepherding means patience.

493
00:50:47,864 --> 00:50:50,114
You wake up at the first light
of the day...

494
00:50:51,040 --> 00:50:53,600
...and herd many animals.

495
00:50:53,662 --> 00:50:56,562
You protect them.

496
00:50:58,539 --> 00:51:01,769
Only with patience, you can bear this.

497
00:51:12,236 --> 00:51:14,696
Waiting takes patience, Mari Hatun.

498
00:51:43,084 --> 00:51:45,094
Alps!

499
00:51:47,559 --> 00:51:49,219
Retreat!

500
00:51:59,542 --> 00:52:01,122
Come on!

501
00:52:02,452 --> 00:52:04,002
Come on!

502
00:52:24,427 --> 00:52:26,117
See how the counters were burning?

503
00:52:26,117 --> 00:52:28,317
We warmed İnegöl up!

504
00:52:28,435 --> 00:52:31,365
The bazaar was in flames.

505
00:52:32,724 --> 00:52:35,854
Long live, Osman Bey!
Long live, Osman Bey!

506
00:52:35,854 --> 00:52:39,724
Stop! Nikola's soldiers are everywhere.

507
00:52:42,879 --> 00:52:45,429
Mashallah to my valiants!

508
00:52:45,669 --> 00:52:47,159
Mashallah!

509
00:52:48,417 --> 00:52:52,137
Where are we going now, my Bey?

510
00:52:54,944 --> 00:52:57,124
Kosses have shown us he is a friend.

511
00:52:57,732 --> 00:53:01,222
Now, the most secure place is Harmankaya.

512
00:53:03,095 --> 00:53:04,865
We are going to Harmankaya.

513
00:53:06,774 --> 00:53:08,824
-Cerkutay.
-My Bey.

514
00:53:10,168 --> 00:53:12,038
Inform Turgut Bey.

515
00:53:12,038 --> 00:53:14,148
Tell him to take Mari and come.

516
00:53:14,803 --> 00:53:17,163
Since we are going to Harmankaya...

517
00:53:17,315 --> 00:53:20,335
...let's have a wedding tonight!

518
00:53:22,783 --> 00:53:24,643
As you order, my Bey.

519
00:53:28,528 --> 00:53:31,978
Alps!
Back to the horses.

520
00:53:37,307 --> 00:53:39,047
Guests need food.

521
00:53:40,668 --> 00:53:42,678
Don't.

522
00:53:43,825 --> 00:53:45,945
You are the guest.

523
00:53:55,731 --> 00:53:57,821
Kumral Abdal.

524
00:53:58,476 --> 00:54:01,006
Can you tell me about your Prophet?

525
00:54:01,787 --> 00:54:04,637
I wondered much more after
getting to know you.

526
00:54:08,472 --> 00:54:10,292
Turgut!

527
00:54:10,292 --> 00:54:12,172
You are hurt!
Are you fine?

528
00:54:12,298 --> 00:54:14,788
I am well, it is nothing important.

529
00:54:18,643 --> 00:54:20,663
O, the healer.

530
00:54:21,409 --> 00:54:23,309
We must take measure.

531
00:54:25,602 --> 00:54:27,372
Come, sit here.

532
00:54:28,165 --> 00:54:29,845
Kumral Abdal!

533
00:54:40,718 --> 00:54:42,878
Don't be afraid, Mari Hatun.

534
00:54:42,963 --> 00:54:45,213
It is not deep.

535
00:54:45,345 --> 00:54:48,295
We will apply ointment and bandage it.
He will be fine.

536
00:55:01,832 --> 00:55:03,892
I am fine, Mari.

537
00:55:04,509 --> 00:55:06,299
Don't worry.

538
00:55:25,269 --> 00:55:26,979
Does it hurt much?

539
00:55:27,085 --> 00:55:29,115
Does the place you touch ever hurt?

540
00:55:29,920 --> 00:55:31,790
Your hands are healing for me.

541
00:55:37,380 --> 00:55:38,900
Now...

542
00:55:39,003 --> 00:55:42,213
...the roads are dangerous.
There are Vizier's men everywhere.

543
00:55:42,817 --> 00:55:44,827
They came after me while
I was coming here.

544
00:55:44,942 --> 00:55:49,312
I got rid of them but soon they'll be here
Kumral Abdal.

545
00:55:56,714 --> 00:55:58,494
I will check outside.

546
00:55:59,489 --> 00:56:01,729
Put the ointment.

547
00:56:02,629 --> 00:56:04,429
Thank you.

548
00:56:08,383 --> 00:56:10,173
Mari.

549
00:56:11,754 --> 00:56:13,854
Now that we are getting married...

550
00:56:15,324 --> 00:56:16,824
... and you are Christian.

551
00:56:18,279 --> 00:56:20,239
I am Muslim.

552
00:56:21,401 --> 00:56:22,881
Have you ever thought of...

553
00:56:23,893 --> 00:56:25,693
...becoming a Muslim?

554
00:56:31,095 --> 00:56:33,066
Is there such a rule to get married?

555
00:56:33,066 --> 00:56:35,746
No, there is no pressure in our religion.

556
00:56:36,745 --> 00:56:39,695
But when I heard you asking about
our Prophet.

557
00:56:41,388 --> 00:56:44,728
No, I love my religion.

558
00:56:48,583 --> 00:56:50,083
Good.

559
00:56:53,405 --> 00:56:55,247
Can we come in?

560
00:56:55,247 --> 00:56:57,107
Come in.

561
00:57:01,146 --> 00:57:03,756
I brought news from Osman Bey,
Turgut Bey.

562
00:57:05,375 --> 00:57:07,165
My Bey told me to tell you...

563
00:57:07,894 --> 00:57:11,724
...to take Mari and...

564
00:57:13,577 --> 00:57:15,967
...come to Harmankaya.

565
00:57:20,287 --> 00:57:22,327
We are having a wedding!

566
00:57:30,366 --> 00:57:32,796
Our wedding is close too.

567
00:57:34,164 --> 00:57:37,824
You are very lucky. I've been waiting
for so long.

568
00:57:37,864 --> 00:57:40,704
I couldn't convince Aygül Hatun.

569
00:57:42,206 --> 00:57:44,806
You are really fast.

570
00:57:48,218 --> 00:57:50,918
I hope you get as you wish, Cerkutay.

571
00:57:51,889 --> 00:57:53,889
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

572
00:58:00,181 --> 00:58:02,371
-Thank you, Cerkutay.
-Thank you.

573
00:58:07,338 --> 00:58:09,078
Thank you.

574
00:58:16,972 --> 00:58:19,002
Why do you look sad?

575
00:58:20,736 --> 00:58:22,766
Don't you want to get married?

576
00:58:22,963 --> 00:58:25,663
No, I want to. I want it so much.

577
00:58:26,418 --> 00:58:28,728
But I am afraid, Turgut.

578
00:58:29,254 --> 00:58:31,383
What if something happens again?

579
00:58:31,383 --> 00:58:34,703
Don't worry, also, we got used to it.

580
00:58:34,962 --> 00:58:39,942
Even if your brother Kosses breaks his
word, I will take you out of Harmankaya.

581
00:58:41,691 --> 00:58:44,011
I'll burn there too, for you.

582
00:58:44,170 --> 00:58:48,380
But know that no one can take you from me.

583
00:58:49,032 --> 00:58:50,972
No one.

584
00:58:54,023 --> 00:58:56,263
Are you ready Mari Hatun?

585
00:58:56,535 --> 00:58:58,345
The wedding awaits!

586
00:59:02,868 --> 00:59:05,448
İnegöl Castle

587
00:59:07,946 --> 00:59:11,136
How could you let this disgrace, Nikola?

588
00:59:11,136 --> 00:59:13,446
I didn't let anything!

589
00:59:13,465 --> 00:59:15,430
I took all the measures!

590
00:59:15,430 --> 00:59:17,885
But Osman...

591
00:59:17,885 --> 00:59:21,827
Osman is running around your castle with
his three alps.

592
00:59:21,827 --> 00:59:23,521
What do you do?

593
00:59:23,521 --> 00:59:25,491
You are right, Vizier Alemşah.

594
00:59:25,535 --> 00:59:28,965
Why are these three alps are out?

595
00:59:30,192 --> 00:59:33,252
Looks like you failed too.

596
00:59:34,767 --> 00:59:37,457
Stop with the excuses, Nikola.

597
00:59:38,486 --> 00:59:41,106
The disgrace outside is your doing.

598
00:59:41,564 --> 00:59:44,714
And we need to find a solution to it right
now.

599
00:59:44,982 --> 00:59:48,274
What solution Kosses?
That bazaar will open!

600
00:59:48,274 --> 00:59:50,354
No, no, no.

601
00:59:51,493 --> 00:59:53,733
We can't fall into the same hole.

602
00:59:56,506 --> 00:59:59,756
Obviously, you can't protect your castle
as you should.

603
01:00:01,264 --> 01:00:05,164
We can't trust İnegöl with such a big
bazaar.

604
01:00:06,724 --> 01:00:08,434
Rogatus...

605
01:00:08,708 --> 01:00:10,808
...you make no sense.

606
01:00:12,270 --> 01:00:14,210
What do you suggest?

607
01:00:14,432 --> 01:00:15,772
Bilecik.

608
01:00:17,205 --> 01:00:20,715
I would never let such a thing happen.

609
01:00:21,934 --> 01:00:24,824
Bilecik is the most suitable spot for
the bazaar.

610
01:00:25,277 --> 01:00:26,957
Even the place of bazaar is ready.

611
01:00:27,304 --> 01:00:28,874
I agree.

612
01:00:30,578 --> 01:00:33,458
The same mistake won't happen again.

613
01:00:34,206 --> 01:00:36,406
The best is Bilecik.

614
01:00:39,759 --> 01:00:42,529
I trust you Rogatus.

615
01:00:45,794 --> 01:00:47,984
The discussion is over.

616
01:01:04,897 --> 01:01:09,157
Why didn't you tell me Osman was coming
to the Söğüt?

617
01:01:10,557 --> 01:01:14,349
So that you could give Osman Bey to that
Vizier?

618
01:01:14,349 --> 01:01:16,299
Hear yourself, Malhun Hatun.

619
01:01:24,484 --> 01:01:26,694
You recognized me as someone bad.

620
01:01:27,521 --> 01:01:29,591
But let me tell you...

621
01:01:30,416 --> 01:01:35,296
...my only goal is to acquit my brother.

622
01:01:37,934 --> 01:01:40,184
If he comes and surrenders now...

623
01:01:41,316 --> 01:01:43,856
... I will go to Konya with him.

624
01:01:44,494 --> 01:01:47,174
But as Osman continues to rebel
like this...

625
01:01:47,437 --> 01:01:49,407
...things will get all complicated.

626
01:01:53,146 --> 01:01:55,396
He ruined İnegöl.

627
01:01:55,436 --> 01:01:58,736
Good for him.

628
01:01:59,121 --> 01:02:01,361
Allah bless his hands.

629
01:02:03,828 --> 01:02:05,708
What are you saying, mother?

630
01:02:08,474 --> 01:02:10,164
Mother.

631
01:02:11,470 --> 01:02:13,790
Osman isn't thinking about anyone.

632
01:02:14,765 --> 01:02:18,605
Because he burnt İnegöl, the Lords came
over me.

633
01:02:19,753 --> 01:02:23,383
They were going to kill me there
if it weren't for Vizier Alemşah.

634
01:02:29,528 --> 01:02:31,888
My life isn't important, mother.

635
01:02:33,366 --> 01:02:35,496
I would sacrifice myself.

636
01:02:36,842 --> 01:02:39,052
What's important is our tribe.

637
01:02:40,579 --> 01:02:42,719
The welfare of our tribe.

638
01:03:08,217 --> 01:03:12,017
You all know very well what will happen
to the tribe...

639
01:03:12,194 --> 01:03:14,344
...if the commerce is over.

640
01:03:16,902 --> 01:03:18,922
Osman must stop.

641
01:03:20,007 --> 01:03:23,357
Otherwise, what he's done will be a big
trouble for him.

642
01:03:23,469 --> 01:03:26,249
There is no day without trouble
for a valiant, Gündüz Bey.

643
01:03:26,966 --> 01:03:30,546
That Vizier you love, support...

644
01:03:30,822 --> 01:03:32,942
...put my father in a dungeon!

645
01:03:40,493 --> 01:03:42,623
What are you talking about, Bala Hatun?

646
01:03:44,298 --> 01:03:48,428
What is Sheik Edebalı doing in a dungeon?

647
01:03:49,711 --> 01:03:52,901
Ask that to your friend Vizier.

648
01:03:55,926 --> 01:03:58,886
I pity you for trusting that Vizier...

649
01:04:00,060 --> 01:04:02,520
...and not your brother.

650
01:04:06,389 --> 01:04:09,149
That Vizier arrested my father
and took him away.

651
01:04:09,930 --> 01:04:12,530
Blacksmith Davud encouraged the people.

652
01:04:12,665 --> 01:04:15,855
People rebelled but, there is no use.

653
01:04:16,204 --> 01:04:18,384
The Vizier achieved his purpose.

654
01:04:18,530 --> 01:04:21,350
My father is now in a dungeon, Gündüz Bey!

655
01:04:25,311 --> 01:04:30,071
If you are strong enough, then first,
get our Sheik out of the dungeon.

656
01:04:42,317 --> 01:04:44,097
Bala Hatun.

657
01:04:53,108 --> 01:04:54,908
I will talk to the Vizier.

658
01:04:56,551 --> 01:04:58,711
Don't worry.

659
01:04:59,307 --> 01:05:03,257
I won't leave my Sheik Edebalı in
that dungeon.

660
01:05:05,944 --> 01:05:08,194
When, Gündüz Bey?

661
01:05:09,161 --> 01:05:11,431
The Vizier is now in İnegöl.

662
01:05:11,976 --> 01:05:14,196
I know he is there.

663
01:05:14,733 --> 01:05:17,243
If he were in Söğüt, I would go to him
now.

664
01:05:17,302 --> 01:05:19,542
But I will, the first thing
in the morning.

665
01:05:24,927 --> 01:05:27,117
If my name is Gündüz Bey...

666
01:05:27,485 --> 01:05:30,015
...I will take Sheik Edebalı.

667
01:06:02,327 --> 01:06:06,277
Julia, you go and get the carriages ready.

668
01:06:07,221 --> 01:06:09,741
As you wish, Rogatus.

669
01:06:16,962 --> 01:06:19,512
Thank you for trusting me, my friend.

670
01:06:19,655 --> 01:06:22,265
This way, we'll get the bigger share.

671
01:06:22,790 --> 01:06:27,200
Of course, you will get the biggest
as the bazaar will be in Bilecik.

672
01:06:28,199 --> 01:06:32,019
But the Vizier is deadly mad at Nikola.

673
01:06:35,364 --> 01:06:39,484
Because his mistake nullified
all the moves of the Vizier.

674
01:06:39,931 --> 01:06:42,961
Now we must strike the fatal hit.

675
01:06:43,479 --> 01:06:45,639
You have to help me.

676
01:06:46,442 --> 01:06:48,852
I will take Nikola for what he's done
to Mari...

677
01:06:49,122 --> 01:06:51,492
...when they enter Bilecik.

678
01:06:51,610 --> 01:06:54,050
I hope that is all right for you.

679
01:06:55,638 --> 01:06:59,768
I just didn't like you involving me
in this.

680
01:07:00,504 --> 01:07:04,864
But the gain you have given me
is priceless.

681
01:07:09,086 --> 01:07:12,656
Also, this Osman.

682
01:07:13,226 --> 01:07:16,144
I want you to take him in when Osman
comes to Bilecik.

683
01:07:16,144 --> 01:07:17,294
What?

684
01:07:17,378 --> 01:07:19,948
He will face the Vizier.

685
01:07:20,153 --> 01:07:23,053
Osman? Are you out of your mind?

686
01:07:23,473 --> 01:07:25,313
In my castle?

687
01:07:25,877 --> 01:07:27,957
You are forgetting, Rogatus.

688
01:07:28,484 --> 01:07:31,854
Enemy of our enemy is our friend.

689
01:07:35,952 --> 01:07:39,222
I can't believe you sometimes, Kosses.

690
01:07:39,953 --> 01:07:43,463
It amazes me what you can do
for your goals.

691
01:07:43,642 --> 01:07:46,452
Don't, please. You saw the risk too.

692
01:07:47,039 --> 01:07:51,279
If we do not act together with Osman,
they will unite and destroy us.

693
01:07:52,761 --> 01:07:55,601
But now, Osman will take the Vizier.

694
01:07:56,259 --> 01:07:57,850
I will take Nikola.

695
01:07:57,850 --> 01:08:01,120
And you will take the gold from the trade.

696
01:08:01,120 --> 01:08:02,530
Isn't it nice?

697
01:08:07,290 --> 01:08:09,390
Let's hope so.

698
01:08:10,123 --> 01:08:12,343
We don't hope.

699
01:08:12,613 --> 01:08:14,513
We make it happen.

700
01:08:56,268 --> 01:08:58,508
Harmankaya Castle

701
01:09:02,647 --> 01:09:04,807
You look gorgeous, my lady.

702
01:09:09,017 --> 01:09:11,206
Thank you Aygül.

703
01:09:11,206 --> 01:09:13,456
This really is a great dress.

704
01:09:15,702 --> 01:09:17,372
Mari...

705
01:09:17,563 --> 01:09:20,083
...what's beautiful isn't the dress...

706
01:09:20,262 --> 01:09:21,942
...it is the one inside it.

707
01:09:24,320 --> 01:09:25,925
Come on.

708
01:09:25,925 --> 01:09:28,545
We don't leave the bride without henna.

709
01:11:15,108 --> 01:11:16,798
May Allah make you happy.

710
01:11:16,936 --> 01:11:18,246
Thank you.

711
01:11:24,225 --> 01:11:25,605
Can I come in?

712
01:11:25,788 --> 01:11:27,288
Come in.

713
01:11:39,552 --> 01:11:40,932
Mari.

714
01:12:21,478 --> 01:12:23,288
You look so beautiful.

715
01:12:26,920 --> 01:12:28,410
So beautiful.

716
01:12:40,863 --> 01:12:42,683
Turgut Bey.

717
01:12:42,921 --> 01:12:44,541
Come on.

718
01:13:07,574 --> 01:13:10,514
Come on. Let's not make them wait.

719
01:13:58,295 --> 01:14:00,715
Vizier, Edebalı is not speaking.

720
01:14:01,125 --> 01:14:02,767
He is very secretive.

721
01:14:02,767 --> 01:14:06,887
But I don't think he knows where
Osman is.

722
01:14:11,231 --> 01:14:14,021
If even you couldn't make him talk...

723
01:14:14,818 --> 01:14:17,478
...he must not know.

724
01:14:18,319 --> 01:14:21,206
Actually, if I could whip him,
he would talk...

725
01:14:21,206 --> 01:14:23,399
... even if he didn't know, but...

726
01:14:23,399 --> 01:14:26,189
...Konuralp came and stopped me.

727
01:14:29,079 --> 01:14:31,829
-Can I come in, my Vizier?
-Come in.

728
01:14:45,031 --> 01:14:46,991
My Vizier...

729
01:14:47,513 --> 01:14:51,193
...Sheik Edebalı is not important only for
Kayı and Söğüt...

730
01:14:51,369 --> 01:14:53,919
...all the Oghuz people respect him.

731
01:14:58,446 --> 01:15:01,056
Torturing him will only lower us.

732
01:15:01,150 --> 01:15:02,790
A traitor is a traitor.

733
01:15:02,903 --> 01:15:07,003
What lowers us is not punishing a traitor.

734
01:15:10,278 --> 01:15:13,688
Konuralp is right, Celali.

735
01:15:18,392 --> 01:15:21,152
We should treat Edebalı fairly...

736
01:15:21,639 --> 01:15:25,429
...even if he is in a dungeon.

737
01:15:27,299 --> 01:15:31,729
We shouldn't distance him from ourselves.

738
01:15:34,159 --> 01:15:39,139
We need Edebalı for our purposes.

739
01:15:44,426 --> 01:15:47,836
You go to Kayı tribe, Celali.

740
01:15:48,294 --> 01:15:53,404
Watch closely. There must be
someone going to Osman.

741
01:15:54,302 --> 01:15:56,812
As you order, my Vizier.

742
01:16:13,490 --> 01:16:16,294
Harmankaya Castle

743
01:16:16,294 --> 01:16:20,234
I bear witness that there is no god
but Allah, and I bear witness that...

744
01:16:20,514 --> 01:16:24,654
...Muhammad (PBUH) is the servant
and Messenger of Allah.

745
01:16:26,882 --> 01:16:30,632
Daughter of Baltu, Mari, do you take son
of Doğan Bey, Turgut...

746
01:16:31,173 --> 01:16:36,743
...as your husband for two hundred
dirhams of gold...

747
01:16:37,370 --> 01:16:39,480
...and thirty sheep?

748
01:16:42,835 --> 01:16:43,875
I do.

749
01:16:43,875 --> 01:16:45,435
Do you?

750
01:16:46,428 --> 01:16:47,788
I do.

751
01:16:49,100 --> 01:16:50,580
Do you?

752
01:16:50,738 --> 01:16:52,378
I do.

753
01:16:55,128 --> 01:16:57,718
Son of Doğan Bey, Turgut...

754
01:16:58,635 --> 01:17:03,345
...do you take daughter of Baltu, Mari
as your wife...

755
01:17:03,408 --> 01:17:05,121
...and confirm your mehr?

756
01:17:05,121 --> 01:17:06,451
I do.

757
01:17:07,679 --> 01:17:10,249
-Do you?
-I do.

758
01:17:10,546 --> 01:17:13,246
-Do you?
-I do.

759
01:17:14,023 --> 01:17:17,593
Do you testify?

760
01:17:21,408 --> 01:17:23,288
We do.

761
01:17:25,855 --> 01:17:29,235
May Allah bless your marriage.

762
01:17:29,379 --> 01:17:30,989
Amen.

763
01:17:38,810 --> 01:17:40,850
O Allah...

764
01:17:41,533 --> 01:17:45,803
...we witnessed the marriage of
these two people.

765
01:17:46,312 --> 01:17:47,884
You witness too.

766
01:17:47,884 --> 01:17:49,434
Amen.

767
01:17:49,729 --> 01:17:52,932
May Allah bless your marriage.

768
01:17:52,932 --> 01:17:54,642
Amen.

769
01:17:54,693 --> 01:17:56,533
Grant love...

770
01:17:57,447 --> 01:18:02,607
...livelihood and perseverance to
this couple's marriage.

771
01:18:02,674 --> 01:18:03,924
Amen.

772
01:18:04,677 --> 01:18:06,317
Amen.

773
01:18:06,649 --> 01:18:11,366
Don't give them lovelessness, discord
and separation.

774
01:18:11,366 --> 01:18:13,086
Amen!

775
01:18:15,301 --> 01:18:17,251
Al-fatehah!

776
01:19:14,197 --> 01:19:15,997
Look...

777
01:19:16,165 --> 01:19:18,751
...Turgut Bey and Mari met after us.

778
01:19:18,751 --> 01:19:21,201
But they are getting married before us.

779
01:19:22,409 --> 01:19:25,129
When will we get married?

780
01:19:25,157 --> 01:19:27,517
Come on, you crazy!

781
01:19:34,526 --> 01:19:36,786
Now that the wedding is done...

782
01:19:38,980 --> 01:19:41,370
...it's time to draw our swords.

783
01:21:41,068 --> 01:21:43,038
Congratulations, Osman Bey.

784
01:21:43,858 --> 01:21:48,948
A superb wedding in such a short time!
Unbelievable.

785
01:21:50,139 --> 01:21:52,069
Don't be surprised, Kosses.

786
01:21:52,680 --> 01:21:57,050
We are always ready for war and weddings.

787
01:21:57,513 --> 01:21:59,243
I see.

788
01:22:15,651 --> 01:22:17,611
By the way, I have good news.

789
01:22:19,110 --> 01:22:21,510
Rogatus is convinced.

790
01:22:22,756 --> 01:22:25,216
He'll take you in the Bilecik Castle.

791
01:22:26,792 --> 01:22:29,322
Vizier Alam Shah!

792
01:22:32,071 --> 01:22:34,441
I'll hunt you down.

793
01:22:35,247 --> 01:22:40,227
And I am going to take revenge from
that dishonest Nikola...

794
01:22:40,483 --> 01:22:42,623
...who tried to kill Mari.

795
01:23:15,207 --> 01:23:16,657
Good luck.

796
01:23:17,870 --> 01:23:21,380
Your breed shall continue.

797
01:23:21,768 --> 01:23:23,788
You have always stood with me.

798
01:23:24,158 --> 01:23:26,168
Thank you Osman Bey.

799
01:23:27,052 --> 01:23:29,102
Thank you.

800
01:23:30,369 --> 01:23:32,219
Mari.

801
01:23:40,057 --> 01:23:42,487
I want you to be happy forever.

802
01:23:42,504 --> 01:23:45,284
Always remember that
I'll always support you.

803
01:23:45,574 --> 01:23:47,944
Thank you for supporting me, brother.

804
01:23:49,159 --> 01:23:51,759
I thought you'd never forgive me
for a moment.

805
01:23:57,152 --> 01:23:58,772
Turgut Bey.

806
01:23:59,872 --> 01:24:03,189
Your breed shall continue.

807
01:24:03,189 --> 01:24:04,999
Eyvallah(thanks) brother.

808
01:24:15,887 --> 01:24:18,537
Good luck, Turgut Bey.

809
01:24:39,638 --> 01:24:43,788
Your tent shall cheer up,
your lives shall be long, my Bey.

810
01:24:43,967 --> 01:24:46,027
Eyvallah(thanks) brother.

811
01:25:02,738 --> 01:25:05,988
From now on, I entrust my sister
to you, Turgut Bey.

812
01:25:08,429 --> 01:25:10,999
I am not going to be worried.

813
01:25:12,054 --> 01:25:13,874
I appreciate that.

814
01:25:18,391 --> 01:25:20,131
Eyvallah (thanks).

815
01:25:42,444 --> 01:25:44,404
What am I going to do with these?

816
01:25:44,691 --> 01:25:46,291
What are those, Cerkutay?

817
01:25:46,291 --> 01:25:47,451
Millet.

818
01:25:47,779 --> 01:25:50,219
You said Millets are necessary
for the wedding!

819
01:25:50,483 --> 01:25:52,291
I found some!

820
01:25:52,291 --> 01:25:54,421
Good, Cerkutay.

821
01:25:54,865 --> 01:25:57,285
You are starting to gain my favor!

822
01:25:59,334 --> 01:26:01,964
Did you just beat me or fondle me?

823
01:26:02,923 --> 01:26:06,323
Come on Cerkutay.
Leave now.

824
01:26:42,719 --> 01:26:44,729
What did Turgut Bey do?

825
01:26:44,729 --> 01:26:47,959
He prepared a feast for his wedding!

826
01:26:48,700 --> 01:26:51,130
What did he do for Mari Hatun?

827
01:26:51,324 --> 01:26:55,944
He butchered stallion, sheep, and ram!

828
01:26:56,395 --> 01:26:58,018
Did he break hearts?

829
01:26:58,018 --> 01:27:01,151
He neither broke hearts nor uttered
bad words!

830
01:27:01,151 --> 01:27:03,901
He married Mari Hatun!

831
01:27:04,836 --> 01:27:08,484
May Allah make them happy!

832
01:27:08,484 --> 01:27:13,454
Amin! You shall be happy!
You shall have a long marriage!

833
01:27:19,153 --> 01:27:20,713
I wish my Boran was here.

834
01:27:22,235 --> 01:27:24,905
My brother's voice is absent, my Bey.

835
01:27:27,455 --> 01:27:28,855
My Bey.

836
01:27:30,641 --> 01:27:32,861
I heard it from Aygül Hatun.

837
01:27:33,778 --> 01:27:35,798
Boran is not well.

838
01:27:38,219 --> 01:27:40,219
What happened to my valiant?

839
01:27:40,691 --> 01:27:42,711
He is going pretty mad.

840
01:27:43,408 --> 01:27:46,018
He is talking to himself.

841
01:27:50,354 --> 01:27:52,644
My mountain-like valiant!

842
01:27:55,974 --> 01:27:57,834
Boran!

843
01:27:59,465 --> 01:28:01,935
Who did this to you?

844
01:28:03,914 --> 01:28:06,154
How could they do this to you?

845
01:28:15,175 --> 01:28:17,135
I can't accept it, Gündüz.

846
01:28:17,616 --> 01:28:19,976
Put an end to this.

847
01:28:21,895 --> 01:28:24,655
I heard something awful today.

848
01:28:25,150 --> 01:28:28,620
Nikola tried to kill Mari.

849
01:28:28,892 --> 01:28:31,212
Turgut Bey was there just in time.

850
01:28:31,787 --> 01:28:35,267
We sent Mari to death with our hands,
Gündüz!

851
01:28:37,116 --> 01:28:40,226
How are going to get rid of this sin?

852
01:28:41,244 --> 01:28:43,444
What if she couldn't run away?

853
01:28:45,831 --> 01:28:50,321
Hatuns keep saying they're going to
find the betrayer who abducted Mari.

854
01:28:50,651 --> 01:28:54,721
May Allah hide our situation.

855
01:29:10,538 --> 01:29:11,978
My Bey!

856
01:29:15,068 --> 01:29:16,798
Are you okay?

857
01:29:18,062 --> 01:29:19,542
I am fine.

858
01:29:22,180 --> 01:29:24,080
Go inside, Ayse.

859
01:29:39,509 --> 01:29:41,949
Hay Masha Allah(praise be) my valiants!

860
01:29:43,585 --> 01:29:45,815
I knew you'd come!

861
01:29:46,692 --> 01:29:48,512
I knew.

862
01:29:51,360 --> 01:29:54,285
I told my Gonca to cook dinner!

863
01:29:54,285 --> 01:29:56,162
She'll be here soon.

864
01:29:56,162 --> 01:29:58,342
We'll eat and eat, my brothers!

865
01:30:02,272 --> 01:30:05,092
If Cerkutay leaves us any food of course.

866
01:30:11,291 --> 01:30:14,121
Come on, have a nice meal!

867
01:30:19,678 --> 01:30:22,918
Bless your hands!

868
01:30:34,140 --> 01:30:35,950
Boran,

869
01:30:40,215 --> 01:30:41,715
Boran,

870
01:30:42,464 --> 01:30:43,985
My bey.

871
01:30:43,985 --> 01:30:45,845
No.

872
01:30:46,997 --> 01:30:49,397
We were having a meal, my bey...

873
01:30:49,406 --> 01:30:51,076
...join us.

874
01:30:57,394 --> 01:30:59,644
You said we were going to talk.

875
01:30:59,980 --> 01:31:01,810
You kept your word.

876
01:31:06,218 --> 01:31:07,838
Yes,...

877
01:31:09,473 --> 01:31:11,143
...I kept my word.

878
01:31:12,347 --> 01:31:14,044
Whose bey am I?

879
01:31:14,044 --> 01:31:16,434
Praise be!

880
01:31:16,499 --> 01:31:18,829
You're Boran's bey.

881
01:31:20,401 --> 01:31:22,061
Kayı's bey.

882
01:31:22,496 --> 01:31:24,466
You're Kayı's bey.

883
01:31:28,236 --> 01:31:31,316
And you are the most valiant
alp of kayı.

884
01:31:31,840 --> 01:31:34,200
You are my most loyal alp.

885
01:31:38,212 --> 01:31:40,072
My bey,...

886
01:31:40,873 --> 01:31:43,293
...I became Gündüz Bey's alp.

887
01:31:45,057 --> 01:31:46,917
I owed allegiance to him.

888
01:31:56,463 --> 01:31:58,053
Good for you!

889
01:31:58,973 --> 01:32:00,823
Good for you!

890
01:32:01,846 --> 01:32:04,576
We trusted you with the kayı's throne.

891
01:32:04,941 --> 01:32:09,201
Whoever sits there, you'll stand by them.

892
01:32:10,696 --> 01:32:13,846
But now that you came...

893
01:32:14,075 --> 01:32:16,025
...I am your alp now right?

894
01:32:19,496 --> 01:32:21,546
I'm going now.

895
01:32:23,033 --> 01:32:26,313
But when I come back, you'll have my back.

896
01:32:27,567 --> 01:32:29,637
Now, promise me that...

897
01:32:30,936 --> 01:32:33,106
...you're going to get yourself together.

898
01:32:33,273 --> 01:32:36,873
Boran, come to your senses.

899
01:32:38,166 --> 01:32:41,746
I'm leaving now, when I come back...

900
01:32:42,265 --> 01:32:44,985
...I want to see you standing strong,...

901
01:32:45,177 --> 01:32:47,267
...fit as a fiddle.

902
01:32:49,300 --> 01:32:52,240
Do you understand my brother?

903
01:32:53,415 --> 01:32:55,515
Yes, my bey.

904
01:33:09,944 --> 01:33:11,924
Brother.

905
01:33:30,900 --> 01:33:32,820
Dear Allah,...

906
01:33:33,344 --> 01:33:35,984
...give me strength to endure this test.

907
01:33:37,697 --> 01:33:40,757
My Osman and now my father.

908
01:33:44,032 --> 01:33:47,042
Help my Osman to overcome
his struggles my Allah.

909
01:33:48,247 --> 01:33:50,197
Help him, dear Allah.

910
01:33:52,909 --> 01:33:54,769
Amen.

911
01:34:18,636 --> 01:34:20,436
Help him...

912
01:34:24,673 --> 01:34:26,463
Bala

913
01:34:30,111 --> 01:34:31,811
Osman!

914
01:34:35,930 --> 01:34:37,660
Osman!

915
01:34:53,912 --> 01:34:55,432
Bala,...

916
01:34:55,730 --> 01:34:57,410
...don't cry.

917
01:34:57,626 --> 01:34:59,046
Don't cry.

918
01:34:59,354 --> 01:35:00,934
Are you well?

919
01:35:01,260 --> 01:35:03,080
Are you well?

920
01:35:03,962 --> 01:35:07,012
We are well, thank Allah.

921
01:35:07,889 --> 01:35:09,929
Don't worry...

922
01:35:10,052 --> 01:35:11,452
...I'm well too.

923
01:35:11,748 --> 01:35:13,618
Your wellbeing is more important.

924
01:35:13,948 --> 01:35:15,810
We're well my Osman...

925
01:35:15,810 --> 01:35:19,850
...we're well but we're going through
Allah's tough tests.

926
01:35:21,319 --> 01:35:24,229
First you, now my father.

927
01:35:26,747 --> 01:35:28,497
I know.

928
01:35:31,662 --> 01:35:33,482
I know all about it.

929
01:35:34,995 --> 01:35:37,035
There is one more thing I know about.

930
01:35:37,846 --> 01:35:40,156
And that, we will see better days.

931
01:35:41,554 --> 01:35:43,754
If Allah permits, my bey.

932
01:35:44,719 --> 01:35:47,009
I also got some good news.

933
01:35:47,075 --> 01:35:51,505
Mari and Turgut got
married in Harmankaya.

934
01:35:52,312 --> 01:35:54,082
Is that so?

935
01:35:56,421 --> 01:35:59,381
I would want to witness Mari's joy.

936
01:36:00,104 --> 01:36:04,034
But it's fate, I guess it
has to be this way.

937
01:36:05,329 --> 01:36:07,929
They are happy now.

938
01:36:09,992 --> 01:36:12,582
Don't keep standing, sit down, my Osman.

939
01:36:12,719 --> 01:36:13,939
No, Bala.

940
01:36:15,755 --> 01:36:17,627
I'm going to speak to my brother.

941
01:36:17,627 --> 01:36:21,927
No way my Osman, Vizier's soldiers
are patrolling around everywhere.

942
01:36:21,982 --> 01:36:24,282
- Don't go.
- Bala,

943
01:36:25,584 --> 01:36:28,044
Do not leave your tent.

944
01:36:29,479 --> 01:36:31,749
Come on, sit.

945
01:36:43,108 --> 01:36:45,118
Be careful.

946
01:38:01,398 --> 01:38:02,848
Traitor,...

947
01:38:04,498 --> 01:38:06,318
...traitor huh?

948
01:38:09,535 --> 01:38:11,185
Traitor.

949
01:39:09,810 --> 01:39:11,410
My brother?

950
01:39:34,317 --> 01:39:36,277
Osman, what are you doing here?

951
01:39:54,390 --> 01:39:56,230
Brother,...

952
01:40:04,788 --> 01:40:07,688
...I trusted you...

953
01:40:07,967 --> 01:40:10,957
...as my brother Gündüz Bey!

954
01:40:29,966 --> 01:40:31,926
Osman, what are you doing?

955
01:41:40,248 --> 01:41:42,058
Gündüz Bey who sits at the throne...

956
01:41:42,630 --> 01:41:45,340
...and makes a deal with a traitor.

957
01:41:46,000 --> 01:41:49,397
Whatever I've done was for
the welfare of our tribe.

958
01:41:49,397 --> 01:41:53,127
Selling out our tribe is for its welfare?!

959
01:41:53,336 --> 01:41:55,436
Being vizier's slave is for its welfare?!

960
01:42:12,307 --> 01:42:16,067
Should we be beys like you Osman?

961
01:42:17,234 --> 01:42:19,854
Should we set the tribe on fire, Osman?

962
01:42:26,032 --> 01:42:30,292
Should we suffer the next pain without
the end of the previous one, Osman?

963
01:42:33,860 --> 01:42:37,330
I saw you at Inegöl.

964
01:42:37,662 --> 01:42:41,152
I saw you and did not tell anyone about it

965
01:42:42,746 --> 01:42:45,706
I don't want any more pain, Osman!

966
01:42:46,688 --> 01:42:49,018
You are making a mistake brother!

967
01:42:49,260 --> 01:42:52,810
If so, you should have told them!
You should have said, "Osman is here"!

968
01:42:53,130 --> 01:42:55,280
You should have stabbed me in the back!

969
01:42:56,052 --> 01:42:59,111
When I saw you with them...

970
01:42:59,111 --> 01:43:02,071
...at that moment you were done for me!

971
01:43:05,122 --> 01:43:07,302
We do business!

972
01:43:08,146 --> 01:43:10,496
We enrich our tribe!

973
01:43:11,247 --> 01:43:13,957
We care for the welfare of our people!

974
01:43:14,449 --> 01:43:16,759
Do you want an enemy?

975
01:43:17,495 --> 01:43:19,775
You don't have a brother!

976
01:43:26,577 --> 01:43:29,017
You disgraced our tribe!

977
01:43:31,136 --> 01:43:36,246
I would have never trusted you
if I had known you would do that!

978
01:43:38,511 --> 01:43:40,251
Osman.

979
01:43:43,022 --> 01:43:44,482
Osman!

980
01:43:48,232 --> 01:43:51,922
Everything you've done was a mistake.

981
01:43:54,186 --> 01:43:56,946
Now, I'm making up for those mistakes.

982
01:43:57,129 --> 01:43:59,279
Now, I'm healing those wounds!

983
01:44:03,225 --> 01:44:05,135
You made a mistake, Osman.

984
01:44:19,046 --> 01:44:20,876
Watch your mouth!

985
01:44:21,740 --> 01:44:23,820
You are afraid of battle.

986
01:44:24,608 --> 01:44:26,228
Only...

987
01:44:27,732 --> 01:44:30,812
...the brave is not afraid of battle.

988
01:44:40,721 --> 01:44:42,581
- Brother,
- Gündüz Bey!

989
01:44:45,982 --> 01:44:48,532
I'm afraid...

990
01:44:48,712 --> 01:44:50,772
...you will end up like my uncle.

991
01:45:17,113 --> 01:45:19,133
My bey, say something!

992
01:45:30,709 --> 01:45:32,699
My bey, we can't come in!

993
01:45:52,830 --> 01:45:55,610
- My bey, are you alright?
- My bey, the door is stuck!

994
01:46:11,219 --> 01:46:12,939
Gündüz Bey?

995
01:46:13,580 --> 01:46:15,090
What is going on here?

996
01:46:31,745 --> 01:46:33,985
That Vizier Alemshah,...

997
01:46:34,205 --> 01:46:37,145
...without dealing with him...

998
01:46:39,288 --> 01:46:42,028
...there is no rest for me.

999
01:46:45,313 --> 01:46:48,673
He has made me so wrathful.

1000
01:46:49,691 --> 01:46:52,171
He will pay the biggest prize.

1001
01:46:53,899 --> 01:46:56,039
I feel you, Osman Bey.

1002
01:46:56,466 --> 01:46:59,226
I hate Nikola just as much as...

1003
01:46:59,641 --> 01:47:02,261
...you hate Vizier.

1004
01:47:02,692 --> 01:47:07,092
Do not worry at all. In the end, both
of us will get what we want.

1005
01:47:07,119 --> 01:47:09,369
Let's not wait any longer then.

1006
01:47:10,024 --> 01:47:11,924
Let's head to Bilecik.

1007
01:47:15,957 --> 01:47:17,607
Osman Bey,...

1008
01:47:20,285 --> 01:47:22,875
...I was afraid I could not catch up.

1009
01:47:23,030 --> 01:47:25,850
If Allah permits, you won't go
without me right Osman Bey?

1010
01:47:28,486 --> 01:47:29,976
No,...

1011
01:47:30,300 --> 01:47:32,370
...this time, I'm going without you.

1012
01:47:32,587 --> 01:47:34,317
You'll stay here.

1013
01:47:34,492 --> 01:47:36,992
Don't leave Mari on
your first day together.

1014
01:47:41,193 --> 01:47:44,113
Horses are with me too,
do not worry.

1015
01:47:45,773 --> 01:47:47,556
As you wish.

1016
01:47:49,156 --> 01:47:51,206
Let's give you a send-off then.

1017
01:48:28,776 --> 01:48:30,416
What is going on in here?

1018
01:48:32,579 --> 01:48:34,349
Where are ahis?

1019
01:48:37,334 --> 01:48:39,494
Why aren't tradesmen
opening up their shops?

1020
01:48:48,709 --> 01:48:52,929
As long as Edebalı is not released from
the dungeon, shops will not be opened.

1021
01:48:55,138 --> 01:48:57,308
You are rebelling...

1022
01:48:57,965 --> 01:49:01,145
...you can't do this, you
can't stop the trade.

1023
01:49:01,167 --> 01:49:04,357
Do you think we will trade after...

1024
01:49:04,837 --> 01:49:07,389
...you capture the Sheik.

1025
01:49:07,389 --> 01:49:09,809
You think you're so smart?

1026
01:49:11,869 --> 01:49:14,129
Sheik Edebalı might be in prison but,...

1027
01:49:15,809 --> 01:49:18,329
...I would not let anything happen to him.

1028
01:49:19,932 --> 01:49:22,352
Whoever harms him will have to face me.

1029
01:49:22,594 --> 01:49:25,394
Where was your mind when...

1030
01:49:25,638 --> 01:49:27,578
...you were capturing the Sheik.

1031
01:49:32,263 --> 01:49:34,363
Take care of yourself.

1032
01:49:36,301 --> 01:49:38,331
Are you for justice?

1033
01:49:39,243 --> 01:49:41,443
Or for unreasoning?

1034
01:50:39,779 --> 01:50:41,919
Vizier Alemshah!

1035
01:50:42,298 --> 01:50:47,548
Your dark dungeons cannot
dim the light of our Sheik!

1036
01:50:49,409 --> 01:50:51,579
Release our sheik!

1037
01:51:04,405 --> 01:51:06,345
Release our sheik!

1038
01:51:12,387 --> 01:51:15,297
Urfan Orhan

1039
01:51:15,942 --> 01:51:19,162
Praise be my valiant!

1040
01:51:19,563 --> 01:51:22,213
Urfan Orhan

1041
01:51:22,272 --> 01:51:24,372
Look at your grandmother.

1042
01:51:24,685 --> 01:51:26,745
Praise be!

1043
01:51:26,847 --> 01:51:28,877
You smell very nice!

1044
01:51:29,738 --> 01:51:31,408
Go to your mother.

1045
01:51:33,467 --> 01:51:35,207
May I come in?

1046
01:51:35,254 --> 01:51:37,674
- Bala,
- You may come in.

1047
01:51:41,782 --> 01:51:43,622
Welcome, Bala.

1048
01:51:43,889 --> 01:51:45,319
Come, my girl.

1049
01:51:46,066 --> 01:51:47,556
Happy to be here!

1050
01:51:49,916 --> 01:51:53,816
Bala, my beautiful girl,
you seem very well.

1051
01:51:55,501 --> 01:51:58,531
Zehra has been taking
care of you very well.

1052
01:51:58,827 --> 01:52:01,227
Yes, bless her.

1053
01:52:01,905 --> 01:52:03,675
She helped me a lot.

1054
01:52:11,803 --> 01:52:13,853
- Mother,
- Yes.

1055
01:52:14,171 --> 01:52:16,051
I got some good news for you.

1056
01:52:16,472 --> 01:52:18,262
What is it, my girl?

1057
01:52:22,128 --> 01:52:23,658
Osman came last night.

1058
01:52:23,743 --> 01:52:25,903
My dear Osman came?

1059
01:52:27,147 --> 01:52:28,947
Osman did come.

1060
01:52:31,967 --> 01:52:35,357
Allah protected him, he did not
get captured by Vizier's soldiers.

1061
01:52:35,373 --> 01:52:36,953
Thank Allah!

1062
01:52:40,072 --> 01:52:42,282
So, tell me...

1063
01:52:42,463 --> 01:52:44,253
...is my valiant well?

1064
01:52:46,030 --> 01:52:48,570
He is well mother, don't worry.

1065
01:52:54,544 --> 01:52:58,554
Vizier your excellence, I got something
very important I want to talk to you about

1066
01:52:58,795 --> 01:53:00,665
Go ahead, Gündüz Bey.

1067
01:53:00,806 --> 01:53:04,546
I've heard what happened, Osman
had apparently broken into your place.

1068
01:53:11,420 --> 01:53:13,170
That is not the issue.

1069
01:53:13,607 --> 01:53:15,347
The issue is...

1070
01:53:15,708 --> 01:53:17,888
...what is Sheik Edebalı
doing at the dungeon?

1071
01:53:18,196 --> 01:53:22,256
Edebalı set us up by colluding with Osman.

1072
01:53:23,460 --> 01:53:26,670
And now serving his sentence
for betraying the government.

1073
01:53:28,176 --> 01:53:30,906
People make mistakes, Vizier Alemshah.

1074
01:53:31,861 --> 01:53:35,531
If he is an occupant, he should
have a chance to redeem himself.

1075
01:53:39,430 --> 01:53:41,670
Can't you see what's going on?

1076
01:53:41,767 --> 01:53:43,777
People are revolting.

1077
01:53:54,250 --> 01:53:58,620
If the son of Ertuğrul Ghazi, Gündüz
Bey wants something from me...

1078
01:53:59,509 --> 01:54:01,759
...I will not turn it down.

1079
01:54:05,646 --> 01:54:07,796
Thank you, Vizier Alemshah.

1080
01:54:08,376 --> 01:54:10,841
It will not happen again,
I vouch for my Sheik.

1081
01:54:10,841 --> 01:54:14,221
Our wish is to gain
the trust of the people.

1082
01:54:14,933 --> 01:54:18,853
If people are angry at us for Edebalı...

1083
01:54:19,558 --> 01:54:22,048
...it means that we have made a mistake.

1084
01:54:26,540 --> 01:54:30,880
Celali, release Sheik Edebalı immediately.

1085
01:54:31,851 --> 01:54:34,291
As you wish, Vizier your exellence.

1086
01:54:43,048 --> 01:54:46,178
I'll release Edebalı but,...

1087
01:54:47,417 --> 01:54:51,207
...I want you to deliver
him to his people...

1088
01:54:54,234 --> 01:54:58,874
...that way Edebalı's trust
towards you will increase.

1089
01:55:01,497 --> 01:55:04,567
I'm heading to Bilecik
for Bazaar, right now.

1090
01:55:05,066 --> 01:55:09,826
And you, after delivering the Sheik to
the people, come to Bilecik Gündüz Bey.

1091
01:55:12,093 --> 01:55:14,163
Allah bless you Vizier Alemshah.

1092
01:55:55,615 --> 01:55:57,445
Alps!

1093
01:55:57,990 --> 01:56:00,350
We will wait for Vizier at Bilecik Castle

1094
01:56:01,694 --> 01:56:04,884
My bey, what will we do with
Vizier after we capture him?

1095
01:56:06,806 --> 01:56:10,016
He made me so wrathful that...

1096
01:56:11,039 --> 01:56:13,829
...I want to rip his lying tongue out...

1097
01:56:14,095 --> 01:56:16,035
...and burn it.

1098
01:56:17,087 --> 01:56:20,567
For the things, he did to the sheik,
I want to gauge his ugly eyes out...

1099
01:56:20,701 --> 01:56:24,221
...and separate his head
from his filthy body.

1100
01:56:24,547 --> 01:56:29,897
I will feed him to jackals so that his
blood does not pollute the ground.

1101
01:56:32,043 --> 01:56:33,663
Allah bless you, my bey!

1102
01:56:33,836 --> 01:56:36,296
But how are we going to
get to the Bilecik Castle?

1103
01:56:48,142 --> 01:56:51,522
We will get there without even
drawing out our weapons Göktuğ.

1104
01:56:55,950 --> 01:56:59,510
We will be waiting for
the Vizier, inside.

1105
01:57:05,726 --> 01:57:08,176
He deserves such a greeting.

1106
01:57:09,605 --> 01:57:10,985
Alps!

1107
01:57:12,056 --> 01:57:13,536
Let' go, let's go!

1108
01:57:21,334 --> 01:57:23,714
BILECIK CASTLE

1109
01:57:29,005 --> 01:57:32,765
Even the Lord is serving his soldiers
under my Bey's command.

1110
01:57:33,514 --> 01:57:35,604
We mean to destroy the tyrant brother,...

1111
01:57:36,130 --> 01:57:38,290
...let no one stand against us.

1112
01:57:39,447 --> 01:57:40,977
Alps!

1113
01:57:42,562 --> 01:57:47,082
To the rooms, to the corridor, disperse
around all sides of the castle.

1114
01:57:49,099 --> 01:57:51,559
I'm going to Vizier Alemshas's room.

1115
01:57:52,221 --> 01:57:54,901
He will be acquainted with
my weapon of justice.

1116
01:57:54,924 --> 01:57:56,824
As you command my bey!

1117
01:57:57,042 --> 01:57:58,492
Come on!

1118
01:58:13,919 --> 01:58:15,949
Vizier.

1119
01:58:22,216 --> 01:58:24,036
Vizier.

1120
01:58:24,535 --> 01:58:28,675
This bazaar will make us a lot of dough.
It doesn't matter where it is.

1121
01:58:29,324 --> 01:58:34,504
As Osman is living as a fugitive,
we will become richer.

1122
01:58:35,203 --> 01:58:39,153
To be honest, I did not expect Vizier
to be able to achieve all of this.

1123
01:58:39,523 --> 01:58:42,673
The order he brought benefited us the most

1124
01:58:45,765 --> 01:58:47,608
The goods are coming tonight right?

1125
01:58:47,608 --> 01:58:48,898
Of course.

1126
01:58:49,257 --> 01:58:52,490
They'll be on the stall by
the morning light.

1127
01:58:52,490 --> 01:58:55,920
There will be a great festival
tomorrow at Bilecik.

1128
01:58:57,288 --> 01:59:00,208
Let's have the Vizier join us.

1129
01:59:44,725 --> 01:59:47,255
Sir, Vizier Alemshah is coming.

1130
02:00:02,919 --> 02:00:06,509
The Vizier of Seljuq State
Vizier Alam Shah.

1131
02:00:34,663 --> 02:00:39,263
Here is the architect of our system.

1132
02:00:40,627 --> 02:00:43,227
We created this system together, Lords.

1133
02:00:43,367 --> 02:00:46,147
We are going to
move together to make it work.

1134
02:00:47,337 --> 02:00:50,087
Absolutely, Vizier Alam Shah.

1135
02:00:51,596 --> 02:00:56,006
This market will contribute a lot to
our economy, thanks to you.

1136
02:00:56,391 --> 02:01:00,483
From east to west, from north to south...

1137
02:01:00,483 --> 02:01:03,323
...Richness will fly into our castles.

1138
02:01:04,277 --> 02:01:07,357
Once we initiate the market tomorrow...

1139
02:01:07,640 --> 02:01:11,830
...we'll see everything about richness,
Kosses.

1140
02:01:24,172 --> 02:01:25,972
Vizier.

1141
02:01:26,970 --> 02:01:29,170
You are going to get what you deserve.

1142
02:01:29,878 --> 02:01:32,548
My Bey will make him pay.

1143
02:01:32,769 --> 02:01:35,609
He'll regret his cruelty.

1144
02:01:37,473 --> 02:01:39,923
His bones will crack!

1145
02:01:43,828 --> 02:01:46,008
May Allah prevent any misfortune.

1146
02:01:47,247 --> 02:01:49,867
My Bey shall settle things at once.

1147
02:01:50,405 --> 02:01:52,515
Vizier has a lot to answer.

1148
02:01:53,490 --> 02:01:57,550
His end shouldn't be quick, Saltuk.

1149
02:02:14,661 --> 02:02:16,321
You have been...

1150
02:02:19,327 --> 02:02:22,237
...covered with the blood of
many cruels...

1151
02:02:30,876 --> 02:02:32,996
...you have been...

1152
02:02:33,889 --> 02:02:36,859
...a nightmare for many betrayers.

1153
02:02:38,000 --> 02:02:39,960
However...

1154
02:02:44,029 --> 02:02:46,289
...however, this one is different.

1155
02:02:49,754 --> 02:02:53,124
May the Creator send us brave enemies.

1156
02:02:55,818 --> 02:02:58,578
This one is two-faced!

1157
02:03:05,200 --> 02:03:07,600
It is my duty to...

1158
02:03:08,889 --> 02:03:11,609
...cut him into two pieces.

1159
02:03:15,883 --> 02:03:17,423
Watch out.

1160
02:03:17,591 --> 02:03:21,821
Your eyes are about to be charmed by the
swords that I will exhibit in the market.

1161
02:03:45,233 --> 02:03:49,303
The protector of our system, Gündüz Bey.

1162
02:03:49,836 --> 02:03:51,456
Welcome.

1163
02:03:51,816 --> 02:03:53,916
Thank you Vizier Alam-Shah.

1164
02:04:00,626 --> 02:04:05,226
Yes, now that Gündüz Bey is here,
we can let ourselves into our rooms.

1165
02:04:05,361 --> 02:04:09,821
We must rest for the market's
opening tomorrow.

1166
02:04:10,207 --> 02:04:13,597
You are right, Rogatus, we should rest
so that...

1167
02:04:13,812 --> 02:04:15,832
...we can wake up fresh.

1168
02:04:15,995 --> 02:04:17,265
Here.

1169
02:04:44,971 --> 02:04:47,141
Every cruel...

1170
02:04:49,076 --> 02:04:51,376
...needs an Osman!

1171
02:04:59,495 --> 02:05:01,635
Come to me, Vizier.

1172
02:05:10,569 --> 02:05:12,539
Come to your end.

1173
02:05:18,506 --> 02:05:20,656
Vizier!

1174
02:05:25,717 --> 02:05:28,987
Gündüz Bey, this is your room.

1175
02:05:30,159 --> 02:05:32,009
Good night.

1176
02:05:33,482 --> 02:05:35,365
This is yours, Vizier.

1177
02:05:35,365 --> 02:05:37,085
One of the biggest rooms.

1178
02:05:47,200 --> 02:05:49,400
We will be here, Hadrat Vizier.

1179
02:06:48,779 --> 02:06:50,069
What's that?

1180
02:06:50,887 --> 02:06:53,287
You are taking deep breaths.

1181
02:06:56,447 --> 02:06:59,507
Did you just realise these
are your last breaths?

1182
02:07:19,978 --> 02:07:22,418
No soldiers...

1183
02:07:23,028 --> 02:07:25,338
...and no slaves that you step on...

1184
02:07:25,900 --> 02:07:30,380
...are available here.

1185
02:07:34,665 --> 02:07:36,495
What are you going to do?

1186
02:07:38,244 --> 02:07:39,954
Vizier?

1187
02:07:40,765 --> 02:07:42,925
What are you going to do?

1188
02:07:45,804 --> 02:07:48,224
Osman Bey.

1189
02:07:51,102 --> 02:07:55,542
I see that my power influenced you.

1190
02:07:56,637 --> 02:08:01,217
You set up a trick to...

1191
02:08:01,774 --> 02:08:04,004
...catch me alone.

1192
02:08:09,009 --> 02:08:10,629
Trick?

1193
02:08:11,466 --> 02:08:14,276
You know about tricks better, Vizier.

1194
02:08:15,170 --> 02:08:17,250
You know about that better!

1195
02:08:20,918 --> 02:08:22,808
However...

1196
02:08:31,816 --> 02:08:34,236
I ruin tricks.

1197
02:08:35,057 --> 02:08:37,197
I ruin plans.

1198
02:08:38,837 --> 02:08:41,937
What is the source of your courage, Osman?

1199
02:08:44,953 --> 02:08:46,893
You have no tribe.

1200
02:08:47,104 --> 02:08:48,854
You have no soldiers.

1201
02:08:49,324 --> 02:08:51,274
You have no power.

1202
02:08:54,031 --> 02:08:58,351
There is no people who would obey you.

1203
02:09:01,200 --> 02:09:04,220
I have faith in my chest...

1204
02:09:05,434 --> 02:09:07,704
...filling me like a breath!

1205
02:09:08,355 --> 02:09:13,035
I have a belief that the Creator stands
with the good!

1206
02:09:24,792 --> 02:09:26,502
What about you?

1207
02:09:28,281 --> 02:09:30,041
What about you?

1208
02:09:31,262 --> 02:09:33,682
You lack it.

1209
02:09:37,459 --> 02:09:39,859
This is why you are afraid.

1210
02:09:40,319 --> 02:09:42,949
This is why you are looking at the door.

1211
02:09:44,591 --> 02:09:48,331
It is not your dare to question...

1212
02:09:48,474 --> 02:09:52,004
...the courage and faith of the
Vizier of Seljuq State.

1213
02:09:52,103 --> 02:09:54,053
Questioning?

1214
02:09:56,792 --> 02:09:59,712
I am going to judge you with my sword.

1215
02:10:01,553 --> 02:10:03,293
Osman.

1216
02:10:03,620 --> 02:10:06,920
Your words exceed your power.

1217
02:10:10,555 --> 02:10:12,995
You may regret tomorrow.

1218
02:10:13,062 --> 02:10:15,552
Let me think about tomorrow.

1219
02:10:18,581 --> 02:10:24,461
You are not going to have
a tomorrow, Alam-Shah!

1220
02:10:30,755 --> 02:10:32,395
You...

1221
02:10:33,319 --> 02:10:36,209
...betrayed Turks' case!

1222
02:10:37,109 --> 02:10:40,869
You clouded the future of Turks!

1223
02:10:43,961 --> 02:10:48,721
You burned that platanus which we
have been watering...

1224
02:10:49,045 --> 02:10:51,185
...with our blood!

1225
02:10:53,844 --> 02:10:55,284
Now...

1226
02:10:55,809 --> 02:10:58,879
Now I am going to burn you too.

1227
02:11:01,548 --> 02:11:03,618
Now I am going to...

1228
02:11:04,092 --> 02:11:07,562
...hang you
on the branches of mighty platanus.

1229
02:11:08,777 --> 02:11:11,217
I shall not be called Osman...

1230
02:11:12,771 --> 02:11:15,121
...if I don't do what I say.

1231
02:11:22,380 --> 02:11:27,050
My sword,
covered with the blood of cruels, ...

1232
02:11:33,420 --> 02:11:36,350
...is going to remove you...

1233
02:11:41,099 --> 02:11:43,679
...from your false way.

1234
02:11:47,388 --> 02:11:49,238
Hadrat Vizier!

1235
02:11:49,813 --> 02:11:51,743
Alam Shah.

1236
02:11:54,754 --> 02:11:56,644
Vizier, are you okay?

1237
02:11:58,801 --> 02:12:00,451
Vizier?

1238
02:12:10,146 --> 02:12:12,356
When the cruels are being cruel...

1239
02:12:15,729 --> 02:12:18,339
...we bring the sword of justice!

1240
02:12:19,848 --> 02:12:21,498
Vizier!

1241
02:12:32,228 --> 02:12:33,848
Vizier!

1242
02:12:36,237 --> 02:12:37,687
Vizier!

1243
02:12:44,680 --> 02:12:53,510
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com